  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Syria Regional Appeal - Lebanon - Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Legal assistance and referrals will be provided to an estimated 7,500 PRL and PRS. Protection emergency cash will be provided to 60 individuals who have faced a protection shock, such as eviction, GBV, or threats to physical security, among other risks. The Protection team will work with UNRWA contracted psychologists to provide community-based PSS for at least 3,500 refugees. In 2024, the Agency will continue to work with 65 community based protection organisations and initiatives supported by UNRWA, involving 500 community members. In 2024, the Protection team will also train 1,000 UNRWA staff on humanitarian principles, gender mainstreaming, GBV, disability inclusion, PSEA, and child protection to strengthen the protection capacity of all Agency services.</narrative>
  </description>
